    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense, I'll try a cautious amount of the blood meal then. Quick follow up though—I've also been noticing some weird, small pockets in the soil where the nutrients seem to just vanish overnight, almost like the compost isn't even being processed right. Is that just a common issue with soil microbes or could something else be going on with the soil structure?",
