      "content": "That rapid disappearance of nutrients suggests a risk of soil alkalization or the presence of heavy metals, both of which can render essential elements unavailable to your kale. Since you noted the soil pH around 6.2 is likely acceptable, the nitrogen loss is more concerning and could indicate nitrogen leaching caused by localized soil compaction or wind erosion. You should consider aerating your planting rows to improve soil structure and ensure compost is breaking down evenly across the entire field rather than just in specific pockets.",
